\DOC IBT_WRAP_TAC

\TYPE {IBT_WRAP_TAC : tactic -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Proves an {ensures} goal about a program whose byte list is an {APPEND} of a
fixed four-byte prefix with an inner program, by reducing it to the
corresponding {ensures} property of the inner program starting four bytes later
and discharging the residual side conditions with a supplied tactic.

\DESCRIBE
The argument {discharge_inner : tactic} finishes off the leftover subgoals of
the reduction, typically by matching them against an available assumption about
the inner program; in the observed traces this sometimes proceeds by
instantiating a previously obtained inner {ensures} theorem and settling the
remaining non-overlapping/offset conditions. Applied to a goal {A ?- t} whose
conclusion is an {ensures} specification for code of the form
prefix-appended-to-inner-program at a program counter, it closes the goal
outright, consuming the assumptions {A}, which in the observed traces are
either an {ensures} statement for the inner program at the shifted program
counter, or separation/bounds facts about the code, stack and output buffers.
{
         A ?- t
   =============== IBT_WRAP_TAC discharge_inner
}

\COMMENTS
In every observed trace the inputs are {ensures} goals of this appended-prefix
shape and the tactic closes the goal outright, so no other kind of outcome is
exercised.

\ENDDOC
